  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )}{3}$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{(1+\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\theta )}{3})}^{2}\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$",
